# H.A.N.N.I. environment overrides and secrets.
#
# V1 needs NO secrets and runs without this file. Copy it to `.env` only if you
# want to set an override below. `.env` is git-ignored; real environment
# variables override values in it. Secrets never go in YAML config or source.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional overrides
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# HANNI_NODE_ID=laptop        # machine label shown in logs and reports; defaults to the hostname
# HANNI_CONFIG_DIR=config     # directory holding the YAML config files
# HANNI_DATA_DIR=data         # logs, database, emergency-stop state (git-ignored)
# HANNI_LOG_LEVEL=INFO        # overrides logging.level from config/hanni.yaml
# HANNI_CHAT_HISTORY=session  # optional: keep dashboard history in memory only; default saves locally

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google login uses the browser and Windows Credential Manager; do not put
# OAuth client JSON or tokens in this file. Run `hanni google login` instead.
# Default grant: calendar.read. Add services with `google login --replace --scopes`
# followed by calendar.read gmail.read drive.read docs.read tasks.read.
# Account defaults are managed by `google use`, not environment secrets.
# Optional path to an existing Qwen3.5-4B GGUF file:
# HANNI_MODEL_FILE=D:\models\Qwen3.5-4B-Q4_K_M.gguf

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional Laya shadow observer (see docs/LAYA_SHADOW.md)
# ALL disabled by default, no model weights or private memory included.
# To use the owner's own Ubuntu Laya GPU over a private SSH tunnel:
# HANNI_LAYA_SHADOW_ENABLED=1
# HANNI_LAYA_TRANSPORT=remote-ssh
# HANNI_LAYA_ALLOW_REMOTE_TEXT=1  # explicit consent for text sent to YOUR SSH machine
# HANNI_LAYA_SSH_HOST=user@your-private-ssh-address
# HANNI_LAYA_SSH_IDENTITY=C:\Users\user\.ssh\id_ed25519
# HANNI_LAYA_LOCAL_PORT=8766
# HANNI_LAYA_REMOTE_PORT=8765
# HANNI_LAYA_REMOTE_COMMAND=cd ~/hanni-laya && exec .venv-rocm/bin/python -m hanni_laya_shadow.server --model ~/hanni-laya-models/laya-general-v2 --port 8765
# Or use local mode with a compatible installed Laya runtime:
# HANNI_LAYA_TRANSPORT=local
# HANNI_LAYA_MODEL_PATH=/absolute/private/path/to/laya-general-v2
# HANNI_LAYA_LOCAL_PORT=8766
